    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Permafrost carbon feedback",
    "problem": "The magnitude and timing of greenhouse gas emissions from thawing permafrost and their impact on climate change remain uncertain, challenging projections because current climate models do not fully account for these complex permafrost carbon dynamics.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a research strategy based on model-data integration, which uses newly synthesized observational data on carbon stocks and fluxes to improve and validate Earth system models, thereby reducing uncertainty in forecasts of the permafrost carbon feedback.",
    "task": "The task is to synthesize current evidence to constrain the magnitude and timing of greenhouse gas emissions from thawing permafrost and to project the impact of this carbon feedback on future climate change.",
